      "description": "Original MIT images, layout geometry and projects by OpenCVDataflowGUI contributors. No customer/third-party images. Three 192x128 views occupy known offsets 0/144/288 on a 480x128 canvas. IDs map received images to calibration records; replay order does not change source blend priority. Missing regions remain uncovered; missing the anchor does not move the canvas. Layout bytes and geometric identity are pinned. Missing-anchor is a deliberate failed partial, missing-error emits nothing, and changed-grid rejects a one-pixel crop-context change. Multiband renders a masked bounded tile. Native-registration fits a new layout as a separate workflow; frozen replay performs no feature matching. IDs/grid metadata assert identity, not physical camera correctness or exposure synchronization.",
